Donetsk.text:
Results of the SBU’s Long-Range Strikes Over the Week:
🔹 Belbek and Saky Airfields in Crimea - Hit a "Nebo-U" radar system and a fuel reservoir;

🔹 Rostov Region - Destroyed a "Grave Stone" S-400 radar, a "Tor-M2" SAM system, and a "Pole-21" electronic warfare system;

🔹 UAV Warehouses - Target struck in occupied Donetsk Region and Crimea;

🔹 Maritime Targets - A "Molniya" missile boat and two sanctioned cargo vessels transporting military supplies between Iran and Russia;

🔹 Filanovsky Oil Production Platform - Hit in the Caspian Sea;

🔹 Oil Infrastructure - "Subkhankulovo" oil pumping station (Bashkortostan) and mini-refineries in Ulyanovsk and Kaluga regions;

🔹Coordination Center in Kherson Region – Up to 100 personnel targeted in a strike involving 13 drones;

🔹Two additional FSB deployment sites – Hit in Kherson and Donetsk regions.

Novorossiysk.text:
The Defense Forces likely hit oil and grain terminals, as well as a Black Sea Fleet base during the attack on Novorossiysk. According to OSINT analysts, the reported damages include:

▪️ The NKHP grain terminal - multiple impacts were recorded on grain silos and transport infrastructure facilities, including elevators;
▪️ A Project 266M minesweeper;
▪️ An unidentified dry cargo ship;
▪️ Coastal infrastructure.

The General Staff reported that the Defense Forces of Ukraine hit four Russian military vessels in Novorossiysk.

Vessels suffered varying degrees of damage:

▪️ two Project 11356 frigates, the "Admiral Makarov" and the "Admiral Essen";
▪️ a Project 21631 small missile ship, the "Buyan-M";
▪️ a Project 22160 patrol ship, the "Vasily Bykov".

Odesa.text:
🇷🇺🇺🇦⚡️ — Toward Odesa, so far this night:   5 Kh-31 missiles, 3 Kh-59 cruise missiles, 3 Banderol cruise missiles, 2 Onyx supersonic missiles, 2-3 KABs, and 3 Shahed-238 have been launched.  @IntelSlava

The attack on Odesa used 6 Su-34, 2 Su-57, and 4 Su-35.

